       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under supervision. A single 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and there is no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is a common regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd advise against it. Once you tell me the dose, I'll enter it right away."
